@* Written in each component, not in an _Imports.razor, whose class Razor makes public (ADR-0201).
   This project's root namespace is ExSheet.MudBlazor, so a plain "MudBlazor" here is this
   namespace, not MudBlazor's, and every product using is written with global:: (the name
   collisions in AGENTS.md). HorizontalAlignment is both MudBlazor's and the engine's; here it is
   the engine's, the one a Cell Format holds. *@
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using global::MudBlazor
@using global::MudBlazor.Utilities
@using global::ExSheet
@using global::ExSheet.Engine
@using HorizontalAlignment = global::ExSheet.Engine.HorizontalAlignment
@using InputKind = global::ExGrid.Chrome.GridInputKind
@implements IAsyncDisposable
@* Not the contract (ADR-0201): MudSheetChrome draws each Toolbar Item with this, and no Consumer
   places it. It is public only because Razor makes every component public, is hidden from a
   Consumer's editor, and may change in any version. *@
@attribute [System.ComponentModel.EditorBrowsable(System.ComponentModel.EditorBrowsableState.Never)]
@*
    A Toolbar Item as the MudBlazor Chrome draws it (ADR-0100): MudBlazor's controls, the same item
    ExSheet describes. A toggle is a MudToggleIconButton, pressed in the palette's primary while the
    Focus cell has what it sets; a menu is a MudButton that opens a MudMenu; a split control is the
    face's MudIconButton beside an arrow's that opens a MudMenu holding the choices, colours drawn as
    Excel's palette ten across. The MudMenu draws no button of its own, and the item's buttons take
    no Tab, so the toolbar stays one Tab stop (SH-50; decided with the user, 2026-10-13). Nothing here
    decides what an item means: every press and choice calls back into the context.

    The wrapper prevents mousedown's default, so a pointer press does not take DOM focus and the
    keyboard stays on the Sheet, as Excel's ribbon leaves it in the cell. The toolbar's keys open a
    list by OpenRequest, as a popover answers its focus requests, and a list opened so takes the
    keyboard into its choices, as the built-in Chrome's does: the choice the Focus cell has, else the
    first that can be made. Its keys are the built-in list's, not MudMenu's: the arrows, Home and End
    move among the choices that can be made, swatches ten across; Enter or Space makes one; Tab keeps
    the keyboard where it is; Escape closes the list. Every key's default is prevented, and none
    reaches MudMenu, whose Escape and Tab would hand the keyboard to its button rather than the Sheet.

    The list is drawn in MudBlazor's popover provider, outside the Sheet, and joins the Sheet's Input
    Order while it is open (ToolbarItemContext.JoinSurface; ADR-0240 section 6, ticket 06): its keys and
    its choices' presses claim their events (data-ex-claims) and are answered in their turn
    (ToolbarItemContext.InOrder), as the item's buttons' presses are, and the keyboard in it is the
    Sheet's. Opened from the toolbar's keys, the list takes the keyboard through the grid (TakeKeyboard):
    the keys typed since the toolbar asked for it are held by the grid until then, and handed to it in
    order. When a list closes — a choice, Escape — the toolbar is told in that input's turn
    (ChoicesClosed), with the keyboard still in the list: it makes the choice and takes the keyboard on,
    back to the Sheet, or, after Escape in a list a KeyTip opened, to its KeyTips (ADR-0100's note of
    2026-10-12), and only then does the list close. The keys typed meanwhile are held by the grid behind
    that input and handed on where the keyboard landed (decided with the user, 2026-10-12), so none is
    the list's, about to go, or the toolbar's — Enter pressed the last item again. Closed by MudBlazor's
    own means, the toolbar is told at once, or once the list has left the page when the keyboard was not
    in it. No script is added (ADR-0021).

    When the toolbar takes the keyboard back while the list may still be on its way (CloseRequest), the
    list closes and a focus not yet given is dropped; a list that was given the keyboard first holds it,
    and closes as any close from here does (ADR-0100's note of 2026-10-12).
*@
<span class="@WrapperClass" id="@Context.Id" @onmousedown:preventDefault="true">
    @switch (Context.Kind)
    {
        case ToolbarItemKind.Separator:
            <MudDivider Vertical="true" FlexItem="true" Class="mud-ex-sheet-toolbar-separator" />
            break;
        case ToolbarItemKind.Toggle:
            <MudTooltip Text="@Context.Tooltip" Placement="Placement.Top">
                <MudToggleIconButton Toggled="Context.Pressed" ToggledChanged="OnToggledAsync"
                                     Icon="@IconOf(Context.Icon)" ToggledIcon="@IconOf(Context.Icon)"
                                     ToggledColor="Color.Primary" Size="Size.Small" Disabled="!Context.Enabled"
                                     tabindex="-1" aria-label="@Context.Name" aria-pressed="@(Context.Pressed ? "true" : "false")"
                                     data-ex-claims="click" />
            </MudTooltip>
            break;
        case ToolbarItemKind.Menu:
            <MudTooltip Text="@Context.Tooltip" Placement="Placement.Top">
                <MudButton Variant="Variant.Text" Size="Size.Small" EndIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ArrowDropDown"
                           Disabled="!Context.Enabled" tabindex="-1" aria-label="@Context.Name" aria-haspopup="menu"
                           aria-expanded="@(_open ? "true" : "false")" OnClick="ToggleListAsync" data-ex-claims="click"
                           Class="mud-ex-sheet-toolbar-menu">@(Context.Text ?? Context.Name)</MudButton>
            </MudTooltip>
            @List(360)
            break;
        case ToolbarItemKind.Split:
            <span class="mud-ex-sheet-toolbar-split" role="group" aria-label="@Context.Name">
                <MudTooltip Text="@Context.Tooltip" Placement="Placement.Top">
                    <MudIconButton Icon="@IconOf(Context.Icon)" Size="Size.Small" Disabled="!Context.Enabled"
                                   tabindex="-1" aria-label="@Context.Name" OnClick="InvokeAsync" data-ex-claims="click"
                                   Style="@SwatchStyle" Class="mud-ex-sheet-toolbar-face" />
                </MudTooltip>
                <MudIconButton Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ArrowDropDown" Size="Size.Small" Disabled="!Context.Enabled"
                               tabindex="-1" aria-label="@($"{Context.Name}, more")" aria-haspopup="menu"
                               aria-expanded="@(_open ? "true" : "false")" OnClick="ToggleListAsync" data-ex-claims="click"
                               Class="mud-ex-sheet-toolbar-arrow" />
            </span>
            @List(420)
            break;
        default:
            <MudTooltip Text="@Context.Tooltip" Placement="Placement.Top">
                @if (Context.Content is { } content)
                {
                    <MudButton Variant="Variant.Text" Size="Size.Small" Disabled="!Context.Enabled" tabindex="-1"
                               aria-label="@Context.Name" OnClick="InvokeAsync" data-ex-claims="click">@content</MudButton>
                }
                else if (Context.Icon == ToolbarIcon.None || IconOf(Context.Icon) is null)
                {
                    <MudButton Variant="Variant.Text" Size="Size.Small" Disabled="!Context.Enabled" tabindex="-1"
                               aria-label="@Context.Name" OnClick="InvokeAsync" data-ex-claims="click">@(Context.Text ?? TextOf(Context.Icon) ?? Context.Name)</MudButton>
                }
                else
                {
                    <MudIconButton Icon="@IconOf(Context.Icon)" Size="Size.Small" Disabled="!Context.Enabled" tabindex="-1"
                                   aria-label="@Context.Name" OnClick="InvokeAsync" data-ex-claims="click" />
                }
            </MudTooltip>
            break;
    }
    @if (Context is { ShowKeyTip: true, KeyTip: { } letters })
    {
        <span class="ex-sheet-keytip mud-ex-sheet-keytip" aria-hidden="true">@letters</span>
    }
</span>


@code {
    /// <summary>The item, as ExSheet describes it.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ToolbarItemContext Context { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>The handlers the list's choices are drawn with, held in fields (AGENTS.md, the Blazor traps).</summary>
    public MudToolbarItem()
    {
        _onChoiceKey = OnChoiceKeyAsync;
        _listDrawn = OnListDrawnAsync;
    }

    // Ten swatches to a row, as Excel's palette lays them out, and as the built-in list moves among them.
    private const int SwatchesAcross = 10;

    private MudMenu? _menu;
    private int _answeredOpen;
    private int _answeredClose;
    private bool _open;
    private bool _giveBackAfterRender;
    // The list closing because the toolbar asked (CloseRequest), which gives the keyboard back itself.
    private bool _closingForRequest;

    // The choices in the order they are drawn — the words, then the swatches — and their elements,
    // by that order. The place the keyboard is on is kept here, moved by the keys, not read from DOM
    // focus, which on a circuit follows a key a round trip behind (ADR-0039's note of 2026-09-25).
    private IReadOnlyList<ToolbarChoice> _drawn = [];
    private readonly Dictionary<int, MudMenuItem> _words = [];
    private readonly Dictionary<int, ElementReference> _swatches = [];
    private int _focused = -1;
    private readonly Func<KeyboardEventArgs, Task> _onChoiceKey;
    private readonly Func<ElementReference, Task> _listDrawn;

    // The list opened from the toolbar's keys, and takes the keyboard once the browser has drawn it;
    // and whether the keyboard has been put in it since it opened.
    private bool _keyboardIntoList;
    private bool _keyboardInList;

    // The list closing from here, in the turn of the input that closed it.
    private bool _closing;

    // The list's membership of the Sheet's Input Order, while it is open (ADR-0240 section 6, ticket 06),
    // and the press that opened it, waiting for it to join.
    private IAsyncDisposable? _surface;
    private TaskCompletionSource? _joining;

    private string WrapperClass => "mud-ex-sheet-toolbar-item" + (Context.Active ? " mud-ex-sheet-toolbar-active" : "");

    // A colour control's face is underlined in the colour it applies, as Excel's is. The colour is
    // the user's choice, document data painted as recorded (ADR-0071).
    private string? SwatchStyle => Context.Colour is { IsAutomatic: false } colour
        ? $"border-bottom: 3px solid {colour}; border-radius: 0"
        : null;

    // The list: a MudMenu that draws no button of its own (no Label, Icon or ActivatorContent), so the
    // toolbar keeps its one Tab stop (SH-50; decided with the user, 2026-10-13). MudMenu's own button
    // carries no tabindex a Chrome can set, and the wrapper its ActivatorContent is drawn in takes Tab.
    // The item's own button opens it, as MudMenu's would; the menu stands at the item's foot, where
    // its list opens.
    private RenderFragment List(int maxHeight) => __builder =>
    {
        <MudMenu @ref="_menu" Disabled="!Context.Enabled" OpenChanged="OnOpenChangedAsync" MaxHeight="maxHeight"
                 AnchorOrigin="Origin.BottomLeft" TransformOrigin="Origin.TopLeft" Dense="true"
                 Class="mud-ex-sheet-toolbar-list" Style="left: 0; bottom: 0">
            @Choices
        </MudMenu>
    };

    // A press on the item's button, in its turn, as MudMenu's own button would answer it: the list opens, or closes.
    private Task ToggleListAsync() => Context.InOrder(InputKind.Click, async () =>
    {
        if (_menu is null) return;
        if (_open)
        {
            await _menu.CloseMenuAsync();
            return;
        }
        // The press's turn ends once the list has joined the Sheet's order, so what comes after it is
        // heard: drawn before it joins, the list is on the page and no press or key on it is the Sheet's.
        // A key typed meanwhile is held behind this press, and a press on the list keeps the keyboard
        // where it was (ListFrame), so it is held there too.
        var joining = _joining = Context.JoinSurface is null ? null : new TaskCompletionSource(TaskCreationOptions.RunContinuationsAsynchronously);
        await _menu.OpenMenuAsync(EventArgs.Empty);
        if (!_open) joining?.TrySetResult();
        if (joining is not null) await joining.Task;
    });

    // A press on the item, or on a split control's face, in its turn.
    private Task InvokeAsync() => Context.InOrder(InputKind.Click, Context.Invoke);

    private Task OnToggledAsync(bool _) => InvokeAsync();

    private RenderFragment Choices => builder =>
    {
        var words = Context.Choices.Where(choice => choice.Colour is null).ToList();
        var swatches = Context.Choices.Where(choice => choice.Colour is not null).ToList();
        _drawn = [.. words, .. swatches];
        builder.OpenComponent<ListFrame>(0);
        builder.AddComponentParameter(1, nameof(ListFrame.Key), _onChoiceKey);
        builder.AddComponentParameter(2, nameof(ListFrame.Drawn), _listDrawn);
        builder.AddComponentParameter(3, nameof(ListFrame.ChildContent), (RenderFragment)(list =>
        {
            for (var i = 0; i < words.Count; i++)
            {
                var at = i;
                var made = words[at];
                var enabled = made.DisabledReason is null;
                list.OpenComponent<MudMenuItem>(10);
                list.AddComponentParameter(11, nameof(MudMenuItem.Disabled), !enabled);
                // The list is closed from here, never by MudMenu's own AutoClose, which hands the
                // keyboard to the menu's button.
                list.AddComponentParameter(12, nameof(MudMenuItem.AutoClose), false);
                list.AddComponentParameter(13, nameof(MudMenuItem.OnClick), EventCallback.Factory.Create<MouseEventArgs>(this, () => PressedAsync(made)));
                list.AddAttribute(14, "aria-checked", made.Selected ? "true" : "false");
                list.AddAttribute(15, "role", "menuitemradio");
                // Noted without a render: a focus changes nothing drawn.
                list.AddAttribute(16, "onfocus", (Action)(() => Focused(at)));
                // A disabled choice hears no click, so it claims none: a click claimed and never handled
                // would hold every input behind it (ADR-0240 section 6). An enabled one claims the keys too,
                // which the list hears in their turn (ListFrame): the nearest claimant is the one asked, and
                // claiming the click alone, it left an Escape typed on it unnumbered, so the key after it
                // reached the list that Escape was closing.
                if (enabled) list.AddAttribute(17, "data-ex-claims", "click keydown");
                list.AddComponentParameter(18, nameof(MudMenuItem.ChildContent), (RenderFragment)(item =>
                {
                    item.OpenComponent<MudText>(0);
                    item.AddComponentParameter(1, nameof(MudText.Typo), Typo.body2);
                    item.AddComponentParameter(2, nameof(MudText.Style), made.Selected ? "font-weight: 600" : null);
                    item.AddComponentParameter(3, nameof(MudText.ChildContent), (RenderFragment)(text => text.AddContent(0, made.Label)));
                    item.CloseComponent();
                    if (made.DisabledReason is { } reason)
                    {
                        item.OpenComponent<MudText>(4);
                        item.AddComponentParameter(5, nameof(MudText.Typo), Typo.caption);
                        item.AddComponentParameter(6, nameof(MudText.Class), "mud-ex-sheet-choice-reason");
                        item.AddComponentParameter(7, nameof(MudText.ChildContent), (RenderFragment)(text => text.AddContent(0, reason)));
                        item.CloseComponent();
                    }
                }));
                list.AddComponentReferenceCapture(19, reference => _words[at] = (MudMenuItem)reference);
                list.CloseComponent();
            }
            if (swatches.Count == 0) return;
            list.OpenElement(20, "div");
            list.AddAttribute(21, "class", "mud-ex-sheet-swatches");
            list.AddAttribute(22, "role", "group");
            for (var i = 0; i < swatches.Count; i++)
            {
                var at = words.Count + i;
                var made = swatches[i];
                list.OpenElement(30, "button");
                list.SetKey(made.Label);
                list.AddAttribute(31, "type", "button");
                list.AddAttribute(32, "role", "menuitemradio");
                list.AddAttribute(33, "class", "mud-ex-sheet-swatch" + (made.Selected ? " mud-ex-sheet-swatch-selected" : ""));
                list.AddAttribute(34, "title", made.Label);
                list.AddAttribute(35, "aria-label", made.Label);
                list.AddAttribute(36, "aria-checked", made.Selected ? "true" : "false");
                list.AddAttribute(37, "style", $"background-color: {made.Colour}");
                // Every swatch hears its click, and claims it; one that cannot be made does nothing in its turn.
                // Its keys are the list's, claimed as on a choice.
                list.AddAttribute(38, "data-ex-claims", "click keydown");
                list.AddAttribute(39, "onclick", EventCallback.Factory.Create<MouseEventArgs>(this, () => PressedAsync(made)));
                list.AddAttribute(40, "onfocus", (Action)(() => Focused(at)));
                list.AddElementReferenceCapture(41, element => _swatches[at] = element);
                list.CloseElement();
            }
            list.CloseElement();
        }));
        builder.CloseComponent();
    };

    /// <inheritdoc />
    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        _answeredOpen = Context.OpenRequest;
        _answeredClose = Context.CloseRequest;
    }

    /// <inheritdoc />
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        // The toolbar took the keyboard back while the list may have been on its way (ADR-0100's note
        // of 2026-10-12): it closes, and a focus into it not yet given is dropped. One that was given
        // first holds the keyboard, which the toolbar's hand-back does not take from it: it closes as
        // any close from here does, and the toolbar takes the keyboard on.
        if (Context.CloseRequest != _answeredClose)
        {
            _answeredClose = Context.CloseRequest;
            _keyboardIntoList = false;
            if (_keyboardInList && !_closing)
            {
                await CloseAsync(null, escaped: false);
                return;
            }
            if (_menu is not null && _open && !_closing)
            {
                _closingForRequest = true;
                await _menu.CloseMenuAsync();
                _closingForRequest = false;
                await LeaveAsync();
            }
        }
        // The toolbar's keys asked for the list (Enter on a menu, ↓ on a split control, a KeyTip); one
        // asked for before the last close request is not answered.
        if (Context.OpenRequest != _answeredOpen)
        {
            _answeredOpen = Context.OpenRequest;
            if (Context.OpenRequest != Context.CloseRequest)
            {
                if (_menu is null || _closing)
                {
                    // It cannot open: the keys held for it are the toolbar's.
                    await Context.ChoicesClosed(null, false);
                    return;
                }
                var standing = _open;
                _keyboardIntoList = true;
                await _menu.OpenMenuAsync(EventArgs.Empty);
                // A list a press opened is drawn already, and takes the keyboard now; one that did
                // not open (its item disabled meanwhile) takes nothing, and the keys held for it are the
                // toolbar's.
                if (standing && _listElement is { } drawn) await OnListDrawnAsync(drawn);
                else if (!_open)
                {
                    _keyboardIntoList = false;
                    await Context.ChoicesClosed(null, false);
                }
            }
        }
        if (_giveBackAfterRender)
        {
            _giveBackAfterRender = false;
            await LeaveAsync();
            await Context.ChoicesClosed(null, false);
        }
    }

    // A choice pressed with the pointer, in its turn.
    private Task PressedAsync(ToolbarChoice choice) => Context.InOrder(InputKind.Click, () => ChooseAsync(choice, escaped: false));

    private Task ChooseAsync(ToolbarChoice choice, bool escaped) =>
        choice.DisabledReason is null ? CloseAsync(choice, escaped) : Task.CompletedTask;

    // Closes the list from here, with a choice or without, inside the turn of the input that closed it: the
    // toolbar makes the choice and takes the keyboard on from the list, and only then does the list close.
    // The keys typed meanwhile are held by the grid, and go where the keyboard landed.
    private async Task CloseAsync(ToolbarChoice? chosen, bool escaped)
    {
        if (_closing) return;
        _closing = true;
        _keyboardIntoList = false;
        _keyboardInList = false;
        try
        {
            await Context.ChoicesClosed(chosen, escaped);
            if (_menu is not null && _open) await _menu.CloseMenuAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            _closing = false;
        }
        await LeaveAsync();
    }

    private Task OnOpenChangedAsync(bool open)
    {
        _open = open;
        _focused = -1;
        if (open || _closing) return Task.CompletedTask;
        _keyboardIntoList = false;
        Joined();
        // Closed because the toolbar asked: it has the keyboard back already.
        if (_closingForRequest) return Task.CompletedTask;
        if (_keyboardInList)
        {
            // Closed by MudBlazor's own means while the keyboard was in the list: the toolbar takes it on
            // at once, from the list while it stands, granted from nothing once it has gone.
            _keyboardInList = false;
            return ClosedByItsOwnMeansAsync();
        }
        // Closed by MudBlazor's own means, with the keyboard on the Sheet or wherever a press put it:
        // the Sheet is asked once the list has left the page, and decides as it does for every Chrome.
        _giveBackAfterRender = true;
        StateHasChanged();
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    private async Task ClosedByItsOwnMeansAsync()
    {
        await Context.ChoicesClosed(null, false);
        await LeaveAsync();
    }

    // The list's frame, drawn by the browser: it joins the Sheet's Input Order, and, opened from the keys,
    // takes the keyboard — on the choice the Focus cell has, else the first that can be made, as the
    // built-in list starts.
    private ElementReference? _listElement;

    private async Task OnListDrawnAsync(ElementReference list)
    {
        _listElement = list;
        if (_surface is null && Context.JoinSurface is { } join)
        {
            var surface = await join(list, null, null);
            // Closed meanwhile, or drawn again and joined by that drawing: this membership leaves at once.
            if (!_open || _surface is not null || _listElement is not { } now || now.Id != list.Id) await surface.DisposeAsync();
            else _surface = surface;
        }
        Joined();
        // Not after the toolbar asked for the list to close: the keyboard is the Sheet's again.
        if (!_keyboardIntoList || _closing || Context.CloseRequest != _answeredClose) return;
        _keyboardIntoList = false;
        var selected = _drawn.Select((choice, at) => (choice, at)).FirstOrDefault(c => c.choice.Selected && c.choice.DisabledReason is null);
        _focused = selected.choice is null ? Next(-1, 1) : selected.at;
        _keyboardInList = true;
        // Through the grid: the keys typed since the toolbar asked for the list are handed to it, in order.
        await FocusChoiceAsync(_focused);
    }

    // The list has closed: it leaves the Sheet's Input Order.
    private async Task LeaveAsync()
    {
        Joined();
        _listElement = null;
        if (_surface is not { } surface) return;
        _surface = null;
        await surface.DisposeAsync();
    }

    /// <inheritdoc />
    public ValueTask DisposeAsync() => new(LeaveAsync());

    // The press that opened the list ends its turn: the list has joined, or will not.
    private void Joined()
    {
        _joining?.TrySetResult();
        _joining = null;
    }

    // A choice took DOM focus by other means than the keys here — a press, Tab from the page: the
    // keys start from it. A place the keys have set is never moved back by a focus landing late.
    private void Focused(int at)
    {
        _keyboardInList = true;
        if (_focused < 0) _focused = at;
    }

    // A key in the list, in its turn: the list claims every key (data-ex-claims), each of which reaches here.
    private Task OnChoiceKeyAsync(KeyboardEventArgs e) => Context.InOrder(InputKind.KeyDown, () => AnswerChoiceKeyAsync(e));

    // The built-in list's meanings, so that swapping the Chrome changes no behaviour (ADR-0100, ADR-0039).
    private async Task AnswerChoiceKeyAsync(KeyboardEventArgs e)
    {
        if (_closing || _drawn.Count == 0) return;
        switch (e.Key)
        {
            case "Escape":
                await CloseAsync(null, escaped: true);
                return;
            case "Enter" or " ":
                if (_focused >= 0 && _focused < _drawn.Count) await ChooseAsync(_drawn[_focused], escaped: false);
                return;
        }
        var across = _focused >= 0 && _focused < _drawn.Count && _drawn[_focused].Colour is not null ? SwatchesAcross : 1;
        var from = Math.Max(_focused, 0);
        var moved = e.Key switch
        {
            "ArrowDown" => _focused < 0 ? Next(-1, 1) : Next(from, across),
            "ArrowUp" => _focused < 0 ? Next(_drawn.Count, -1) : Next(from, -across),
            "ArrowRight" when across > 1 => Next(from, 1),
            "ArrowLeft" when across > 1 => Next(from, -1),
            "Home" => Next(-1, 1),
            "End" => Next(_drawn.Count, -1),
            _ => _focused,
        };
        if (moved == _focused) return;
        _focused = moved;
        await FocusChoiceAsync(_focused);
    }

    // The next choice from `from` that can be made, `step` at a time; `from` itself when none is.
    private int Next(int from, int step)
    {
        for (var at = from + step; at >= 0 && at < _drawn.Count; at += step)
        {
            if (_drawn[at].DisabledReason is null) return at;
        }
        return Math.Clamp(from, 0, Math.Max(0, _drawn.Count - 1));
    }

    // The keyboard to a choice, through the Sheet's grid (ToolbarItemContext.TakeKeyboard): granted while the
    // keyboard is the Sheet's, in the list or on the toolbar, so a press the user made elsewhere keeps it.
    private async Task FocusChoiceAsync(int at)
    {
        ElementReference element;
        if (_words.TryGetValue(at, out var word)) element = word.ElementReference;
        else if (!_swatches.TryGetValue(at, out element)) return;
        if (element.Context is null) return;
        try
        {
            await Context.TakeKeyboard(element);
        }
        catch (Exception ex) when (ex is Microsoft.JSInterop.JSException or Microsoft.JSInterop.JSDisconnectedException or ObjectDisposedException or OperationCanceledException)
        {
            // The list closed, or the circuit went, between the render and the focus.
        }
    }

    private static string? IconOf(ToolbarIcon icon) => icon switch
    {
        ToolbarIcon.Bold => Icons.Material.Filled.FormatBold,
        ToolbarIcon.Italic => Icons.Material.Filled.FormatItalic,
        ToolbarIcon.Underline => Icons.Material.Filled.FormatUnderlined,
        ToolbarIcon.Strikethrough => Icons.Material.Filled.StrikethroughS,
        ToolbarIcon.FontColour => Icons.Material.Filled.FormatColorText,
        ToolbarIcon.Fill => Icons.Material.Filled.FormatColorFill,
        ToolbarIcon.Borders => Icons.Material.Filled.BorderBottom,
        ToolbarIcon.AlignLeft => Icons.Material.Filled.FormatAlignLeft,
        ToolbarIcon.AlignCenter => Icons.Material.Filled.FormatAlignCenter,
        ToolbarIcon.AlignRight => Icons.Material.Filled.FormatAlignRight,
        ToolbarIcon.Percent => Icons.Material.Filled.Percent,
        ToolbarIcon.FormatCells => Icons.Material.Outlined.TableChart,
        _ => null,
    };

    // Material has no picture for the comma style; it shows Excel's.
    private static string? TextOf(ToolbarIcon icon) => icon == ToolbarIcon.Comma ? "," : null;

    // The list's frame inside MudBlazor's popover, which its provider draws in a render of its own:
    // its first OnAfterRender is the moment the browser has the choices on the page. It claims the
    // list's keys (data-ex-claims) and hears every one, preventing its default and keeping it from
    // MudMenu, whose Escape and Tab would hand the keyboard to its button rather than the Sheet; it
    // draws nothing for them: a key moves the keyboard, or closes the list from the item. A press in it
    // leaves the keyboard where it was, as a press on the built-in list does: on the Sheet when the
    // pointer opened the list, where a key typed after the choice is the Sheet's whether or not the list
    // had joined yet.
    private sealed class ListFrame : ComponentBase, IHandleEvent
    {
        private ElementReference _element;

        [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

        [Parameter] public Func<KeyboardEventArgs, Task>? Key { get; set; }

        [Parameter] public Func<ElementReference, Task>? Drawn { get; set; }

        protected override void BuildRenderTree(Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Rendering.RenderTreeBuilder builder)
        {
            builder.OpenElement(0, "div");
            builder.AddAttribute(1, "class", "mud-ex-sheet-toolbar-choices");
            builder.AddAttribute(2, "role", "none");
            builder.AddAttribute(3, "data-ex-claims", "keydown");
            builder.AddAttribute(4, "onkeydown", EventCallback.Factory.Create<KeyboardEventArgs>(this, OnKeyAsync));
            builder.AddEventPreventDefaultAttribute(5, "onkeydown", true);
            builder.AddEventStopPropagationAttribute(6, "onkeydown", true);
            builder.AddEventPreventDefaultAttribute(7, "onmousedown", true);
            builder.AddElementReferenceCapture(8, element => _element = element);
            builder.AddContent(9, ChildContent);
            builder.CloseElement();
        }

        private Task OnKeyAsync(KeyboardEventArgs e) => Key?.Invoke(e) ?? Task.CompletedTask;

        Task IHandleEvent.HandleEventAsync(EventCallbackWorkItem callback, object? arg) => callback.InvokeAsync(arg);

        protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
        {
            if (firstRender && Drawn is { } drawn) await drawn(_element);
        }
    }
}
